IMPORT prelude

-- Republic of Singapore Independence Act 1965 (Singapore) -- Singapore Day (s 1), who exercises executive authority (s 4), which
-- provisions of the Constitution of Malaysia stopped applying (s 6(3)) and who now exercises the powers of those that continue
-- (s 6(4)), including the make-up of the Legal Service Commission (s 6(4)(f)); the official and national languages (s 7); the
-- President's power of pardon and the death-sentence report route (s 8); the return of public officers (s 10); appeals from the
-- High Court (s 11); Malaysian members of statutory boards (s 12); and how existing laws are read and modified (s 13).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RSIA1965.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Its Legislative History lists only
-- Act 9 of 1965, Act 7 of 1972 (the Singapore Armed Forces Act, which deleted the 1985 Edition's s 8(3)) and the 1985 Revised
-- Edition. Section numbers here follow the BODY (ss 1 to 14); the arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is printed one
-- line out of step with it.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0258 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For an ordinary person the answer is short: the languages they may use (s 7), how clemency works if they
-- are convicted (s 8), and, for anyone reading an old law, how its references to Malaysian offices are read today (s 13(2)).
--
-- Not encoded: the vesting provisions as such (ss 3, 5, 9) beyond what s 6(4) and s 13(2) say; s 6(1), (2) and (5) beyond the
-- s 6(3) list; which Articles of the Constitution of Malaysia fall within the Parts listed in s 6(3) (the deposit does not say, so
-- it is a flag); s 13(5) to (7) beyond their effect on the tests; and the saving in s 14.
--
-- DATES are written as numbers of the form YYYYMMDD (9 August 1965 is 19650809), so that "on or after" is AT LEAST. That is an
-- encoding convention, not the Act's.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Republic of Singapore Independence Act 1965`

§§ `1 -- Singapore Day`

-- s 1: the Act "shall be deemed to have come into operation on the 9th day of August 1965 (hereinafter in this Act referred to as
-- 'Singapore Day')". The Legislative History (which says it "is not part of the Act") gives the Second Reading as 22 December 1965.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Singapore Day` MEANS 19650809

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act is in operation on` IF `the date` AT LEAST `Singapore Day`

§§ `4 -- executive authority`

-- s 4: "The executive authority of Singapore shall, on and after Singapore Day, be vested in the Head of State and shall be
-- exercisable by him or by the Cabinet or by any Minister authorised by the Cabinet." s 2: "Head of State" means the President.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `the President`
    `the Cabinet`
    `a Minister authorised by the Cabinet`
    `a Minister not authorised by the Cabinet`
    `a Permanent Secretary`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may exercise the executive authority` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `the President` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Cabinet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Minister authorised by the Cabinet` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6(3) -- provisions of the Constitution of Malaysia that ceased to have effect`

-- s 6(1): the Constitution of Malaysia, "other than those set out in subsection (3), shall continue in force in Singapore", modified
-- to fit independence. s 6(3): these "shall cease to have effect in Singapore": "Part I; Article 13; Articles 14 to 18; Article 19A;
-- Article 22; Articles 28 and 28A; Articles 30, 30A and 30B; Part IV; Part V; Part VI; Part VII; Part VIII; Articles 133 and 134;
-- Article 139; Articles 141 to 143; Articles 146A to 148; Part XII; Part XIII; Part XIV" and the Third, Fourth, Fifth, Seventh,
-- Eighth, Ninth, Tenth, Eleventh and Thirteenth Schedules.
--
-- An Article is given as its number and its letter suffix ("" for none). Whether it sits in a listed Part is a flag, because the
-- deposit does not reproduce the Constitution of Malaysia. "Articles 146A to 148" is read as every lettered Article 146 plus 147
-- and 148, but not Article 146 itself: that is an inference from the range's starting point.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER, `to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is between` IF n AT LEAST `from` AND n AT MOST `to`

GIVEN `article` IS A NUMBER, `suffix` IS A STRING, `the Article is in a Part listed in s 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Article ceased to have effect in Singapore` IF
        `the Article is in a Part listed in s 6(3)`
    OR  (    `suffix` EQUALS ""
         AND (   `article` EQUALS 13
              OR `is between` `article` 14 18
              OR `article` EQUALS 22
              OR `article` EQUALS 28
              OR `article` EQUALS 30
              OR `article` EQUALS 133
              OR `article` EQUALS 134
              OR `article` EQUALS 139
              OR `is between` `article` 141 143
              OR `is between` `article` 147 148))
    OR  (`article` EQUALS 19 AND `suffix` EQUALS "A")
    OR  (`article` EQUALS 28 AND `suffix` EQUALS "A")
    OR  (`article` EQUALS 30 AND (`suffix` EQUALS "A" OR `suffix` EQUALS "B"))
    OR  (`article` EQUALS 146 AND (NOT (`suffix` EQUALS "")))

§§ `6(4) -- who exercises the continued Malaysian constitutional powers`

-- s 6(4): the powers conferred by the continued provisions "shall be exercised on and after Singapore Day as follows": (a) Yang
-- di-Pertuan Agong -> the President; (b) Federal Government -> the Government of Singapore; (c) Federal Legislature -> the Legislature
-- of Singapore; (d) Prime Minister of Malaysia -> the Prime Minister of Singapore; (e) a Minister of Malaysia -> "the corresponding
-- Minister in Singapore or by such Minister as may be designated by the Prime Minister of Singapore"; (f) Judicial and Legal Service
-- Commission -> a Legal Service Commission; (g) "the powers of the Police Force Commission shall be exercised by the Public Service
-- Commission"; (h) Lord President of the Federal Court -> the Chief Justice of Singapore; (i) Attorney-General of Malaysia -> the
-- Attorney-General of Singapore.
DECLARE MalaysianHolder IS ONE OF
    `the Yang di-Pertuan Agong`
    `the Federal Government`
    `the Federal Legislature`
    `the Prime Minister of Malaysia`
    `a Minister of Malaysia`
    `the Judicial and Legal Service Commission`
    `the Police Force Commission`
    `the Lord President of the Federal Court`
    `the Attorney-General of Malaysia`

GIVEN `the holder` IS A MalaysianHolder
GIVETH A STRING
`who now exercises the powers of` `the holder` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the holder`
    WHEN `the Yang di-Pertuan Agong` THEN "the President"
    WHEN `the Federal Government` THEN "the Government of Singapore"
    WHEN `the Federal Legislature` THEN "the Legislature of Singapore"
    WHEN `the Prime Minister of Malaysia` THEN "the Prime Minister of Singapore"
    WHEN `a Minister of Malaysia` THEN "the corresponding Minister in Singapore, or a Minister designated by the Prime Minister"
    WHEN `the Judicial and Legal Service Commission` THEN "the Legal Service Commission"
    WHEN `the Police Force Commission` THEN "the Public Service Commission"
    WHEN `the Lord President of the Federal Court` THEN "the Chief Justice of Singapore"
    WHEN `the Attorney-General of Malaysia` THEN "the Attorney-General of Singapore"

-- s 6(4)(f): the Legal Service Commission "shall consist of the following persons: (i) the Chief Justice, as President; (ii) the
-- Attorney-General; (iii) the Chairman of the Public Service Commission; (iv) a Judge of the High Court nominated generally or
-- specially by the Chief Justice; and (v) not more than 2 members of the Public Service Commission nominated generally or specially
-- by the Chairman of the Public Service Commission".
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the Chief Justice`
    `the Attorney-General`
    `the Chairman of the Public Service Commission`
    `a High Court Judge nominated by the Chief Justice`
    `a High Court Judge not nominated`
    `a PSC member nominated by the PSC Chairman`
    `a PSC member not nominated`
    `a Minister`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sit on the Legal Service Commission` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the Chief Justice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Attorney-General` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Chairman of the Public Service Commission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a High Court Judge nominated by the Chief Justice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a PSC member nominated by the PSC Chairman` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `presides over the Legal Service Commission` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the Chief Justice` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (iv) speaks of "a Judge" and (v) of "not more than 2" members. Counting the seats to a maximum of 6 is an inference from that.
GIVEN `nominated judges` IS A NUMBER, `nominated PSC members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Legal Service Commission is lawfully composed` IF
    `nominated judges` EQUALS 1 AND `nominated PSC members` AT MOST 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest Legal Service Commission` MEANS 3 PLUS 1 PLUS 2

§§ `7 -- languages`

-- s 7(1): "Malay, Mandarin, Tamil and English shall be the 4 official languages in Singapore." (2): "The national language shall be
-- the Malay language and shall be in the Roman script: Provided that -- (a) no person shall be prohibited or prevented from using or
-- from teaching or learning any other language; and (b) nothing in this section shall prejudice the right of the Government to
-- preserve and sustain the use and study of the language of any other community in Singapore."
DECLARE Language IS ONE OF
    `Malay`
    `Mandarin`
    `Tamil`
    `English`
    `Hokkien`
    `Hindi`
    `Japanese`

GIVEN `the language` IS A Language
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an official language` IF
    CONSIDER `the language`
    WHEN `Malay` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Mandarin` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Tamil` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `English` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the language` IS A Language
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the national language` IF
    CONSIDER `the language`
    WHEN `Malay` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The proviso is not limited to official languages: "any other language".
GIVEN `the language` IS A Language
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no one may be prevented from using, teaching or learning` IF TRUE

§§ `8 -- pardon, reprieve, respite and remission`

-- s 8(1): "The President, as occasion shall arise, may, on the advice of the Cabinet -- (a) grant a pardon to any accomplice in any
-- offence who gives information which leads to the conviction of the principal offender or any one of the principal offenders, if
-- more than one; (b) grant to any offender convicted of any offence in any court in Singapore, a pardon, free or subject to lawful
-- conditions, or any reprieve or respite, either indefinite or for such period as the President may think fit, of the execution of
-- any sentence pronounced on such offender; or (c) remit the whole or any part of such sentence or of any penalty or forfeiture
-- imposed by law."
--
-- (a) does not require the accomplice to have been convicted. "Such sentence" in (c) is read as the sentence in (b), so remitting a
-- sentence needs a conviction in a Singapore court; "any penalty or forfeiture imposed by law" is read as not needing one. Both
-- readings are the encoder's.
DECLARE Clemency IS ONE OF
    `a pardon to an informing accomplice`
    `a free pardon`
    `a conditional pardon`
    `a reprieve`
    `a respite`
    `remission of a sentence`
    `remission of a penalty or forfeiture`

GIVEN `the clemency` IS A Clemency,
      `on the advice of the Cabinet` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an accomplice whose information led to convicting a principal offender` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `convicted by a court in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may grant` IF
        `on the advice of the Cabinet`
    AND CONSIDER `the clemency`
        WHEN `a pardon to an informing accomplice` THEN `an accomplice whose information led to convicting a principal offender`
        WHEN `remission of a penalty or forfeiture` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `convicted by a court in Singapore`

-- s 8(2): where an offender "has been condemned to death by the sentence of any court and in the event of an appeal such sentence has
-- been confirmed by the appellate court", the President "shall cause the reports which are made to him by the Judge who tried the
-- case and the Chief Justice or other presiding Judge of the appellate court to be forwarded to the Attorney-General", and "after
-- the Attorney-General has given his opinion thereon, the reports shall be sent, together with the Attorney-General's opinion, to the
-- Cabinet so that the Cabinet may advise the President".
--
-- On its words the route is triggered only where there was an appeal and the sentence was confirmed. A death sentence that was not
-- appealed is outside s 8(2); the text does not say what happens then.
GIVEN `sentenced to death` IS A BOOLEAN, `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `confirmed on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 8(2) report route applies` IF
    `sentenced to death` AND `appealed` AND `confirmed on appeal`

DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `the trial Judge and the appellate presiding Judge report to the President`
    `the President forwards the reports to the Attorney-General`
    `the Attorney-General gives an opinion`
    `the reports and the opinion are sent to the Cabinet`
    `the Cabinet advises the President`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A Step
`the step after` `the step` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `the trial Judge and the appellate presiding Judge report to the President` THEN `the President forwards the reports to the Attorney-General`
    WHEN `the President forwards the reports to the Attorney-General` THEN `the Attorney-General gives an opinion`
    WHEN `the Attorney-General gives an opinion` THEN `the reports and the opinion are sent to the Cabinet`
    WHEN `the reports and the opinion are sent to the Cabinet` THEN `the Cabinet advises the President`
    OTHERWISE `the Cabinet advises the President`

§§ `10 -- public officers`

-- s 10(1): persons who "immediately before 16 September 1963 were officers employed by the Government of Singapore and who on that day
-- or after became officers employed by the Government of Malaysia shall on Singapore Day become once again officers employed by the
-- Government of Singapore". (2): persons who "between 16 September 1963 and Singapore Day were engaged by the Government of Malaysia
-- and were employed in those departments which were departments of the Government of Singapore before 16 September 1963 shall on
-- Singapore Day become persons temporarily employed by the Government of Singapore". (3): "The President may within 24 months of
-- Singapore Day confirm or terminate the employment of any person or class of persons who are temporarily employed by the Government
-- under the provisions of subsection (2)."
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `once again a Singapore Government officer`
    `temporarily employed by the Singapore Government`
    `not transferred by s 10`

GIVEN `a Singapore officer before 16 September 1963` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `became a Malaysian Government officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `engaged by Malaysia between 16 September 1963 and Singapore Day` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in a former Singapore department` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Status
`status on Singapore Day` `a Singapore officer before 16 September 1963` `became a Malaysian Government officer` `engaged by Malaysia between 16 September 1963 and Singapore Day` `in a former Singapore department` MEANS
    IF `a Singapore officer before 16 September 1963` AND `became a Malaysian Government officer`
    THEN `once again a Singapore Government officer`
    ELSE IF `engaged by Malaysia between 16 September 1963 and Singapore Day` AND `in a former Singapore department`
         THEN `temporarily employed by the Singapore Government`
         ELSE `not transferred by s 10`

-- "Within 24 months of Singapore Day" is taken to run to 9 August 1967 inclusive; whether the last day counts is the encoder's
-- reading, and no test sits on it.
GIVEN `the status` IS A Status, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may confirm or terminate under s 10(3)` IF
        CONSIDER `the status`
        WHEN `temporarily employed by the Singapore Government` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    AND `the date` AT MOST 19670809

§§ `11 -- appeals from the High Court`

-- s 11: "Until other provision is made by the Legislature, the jurisdiction ... and the practice and procedure of the High Court and
-- the subordinate courts of Singapore shall be the same as that exercised and followed immediately before Singapore Day, and appeals
-- from the High Court shall continue to lie to the Federal Court of Malaysia and to the Privy Council." The 2020 Revised Edition
-- still prints this. Whether the Legislature has made other provision is not something this deposit says; it is a flag.
GIVEN `the Legislature has made other provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `appeals from the High Court lie to the Federal Court of Malaysia and the Privy Council` IF
    NOT `the Legislature has made other provision`

§§ `12 -- Malaysian members of statutory boards`

-- s 12: a provision of written law enabling a board member "to be appointed from Malaysia or as representing any authority or person
-- or body of persons in Malaysia shall, unless the President by notification in the Gazette otherwise orders, cease to have effect
-- and such statutory board or body shall be deemed to be properly constituted notwithstanding that no such member has been or is
-- appointed".
GIVEN `the President has ordered otherwise by Gazette notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provision for a Malaysian member still has effect` IF
    `the President has ordered otherwise by Gazette notification`

GIVEN `the President has ordered otherwise by Gazette notification` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Malaysian member has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board is deemed properly constituted` IF
    (NOT `the President has ordered otherwise by Gazette notification`) OR `a Malaysian member has been appointed`

§§ `13 -- existing laws`

-- s 13(1): "all existing laws shall continue in force on and after Singapore Day", construed to conform with the Act and
-- independence. (2): in any existing law, "unless the context otherwise requires": (a) the Colony or the State of Singapore -> the
-- Republic of Singapore; (b) the Yang di-Pertuan Agong -> the President; (c) the Yang di-Pertuan Negara -> the President; (d) the
-- Cabinet, the Prime Minister or a Minister of Malaysia -> the Cabinet, the Prime Minister or the appropriate Minister of Singapore;
-- (e) the Parliament or House of Representatives of Malaysia -> the Parliament of Singapore; (f) the Legislative Assembly -> the
-- Parliament of Singapore; (g) the Attorney-General of Malaysia -> the Attorney-General of Singapore; (h) the State Advocate-General
-- of Singapore -> the Attorney-General of Singapore; (i) a Malaysian public office or body -> the corresponding Singapore officer or
-- body. (5): the Prime Minister may by order declare the appropriate Minister and the corresponding officer or body.
-- (7): "'existing law' means any law including written law having effect as part of the law of Singapore prior to Singapore Day".
DECLARE Reference IS ONE OF
    `the Colony of Singapore`
    `the State of Singapore`
    `the Yang di-Pertuan Agong in an old law`
    `the Yang di-Pertuan Negara`
    `the Prime Minister of Malaysia in an old law`
    `the House of Representatives of Malaysia`
    `the Legislative Assembly`
    `the Attorney-General of Malaysia in an old law`
    `the State Advocate-General of Singapore`
    `a Malaysian public office`

GIVEN `the reference` IS A Reference
GIVETH A STRING
`how an existing law's reference is read` `the reference` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reference`
    WHEN `the Colony of Singapore` THEN "the Republic of Singapore"
    WHEN `the State of Singapore` THEN "the Republic of Singapore"
    WHEN `the Yang di-Pertuan Agong in an old law` THEN "the President"
    WHEN `the Yang di-Pertuan Negara` THEN "the President"
    WHEN `the Prime Minister of Malaysia in an old law` THEN "the Prime Minister of Singapore"
    WHEN `the House of Representatives of Malaysia` THEN "the Parliament of Singapore"
    WHEN `the Legislative Assembly` THEN "the Parliament of Singapore"
    WHEN `the Attorney-General of Malaysia in an old law` THEN "the Attorney-General of Singapore"
    WHEN `the State Advocate-General of Singapore` THEN "the Attorney-General of Singapore"
    WHEN `a Malaysian public office` THEN "the corresponding public officer of Singapore, as the Prime Minister may declare"

GIVEN `took effect on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an existing law` IF `took effect on` LESS THAN `Singapore Day`

-- s 13(3)(a): the President may by order "made at any time during the period of 3 years after the coming into operation of this Act"
-- make modifications in any written law consequent on the Act and on independence; (c) an order "shall have effect from such date,
-- not being earlier than Singapore Day, as may be specified therein"; (d) presented to Parliament "as soon as possible".
-- (4): "Without prejudice to the generality of the powers contained in subsection (3), the President may by order make such
-- modifications in any written law as appear to him to be necessary or expedient in consequence of the abolition of the City
-- Council and of the Rural Board". Subsection (4) states no time limit; reading that as no 3-year window is the encoder's inference.
-- The 3-year window is taken to end on 9 August 1968 inclusive; no test sits on the last day. Paragraph (c) is about "an order made
-- under this subsection", that is (3), so it is not applied to an order under (4): again the encoder's reading.
GIVEN `made on` IS A NUMBER, `effective from` IS A NUMBER, `consequent on abolishing the City Council and Rural Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a modification order is valid in time` IF
        `consequent on abolishing the City Council and Rural Board`
    OR  (`made on` AT MOST 19680809 AND `effective from` AT LEAST `Singapore Day`)
